    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Hidden shares enumerated ($-suffix names)", "technique": "T1564", "what_happened": "At 2032-09-12 03:14:08 UTC, Sysmon EID 1 reports powershell.exe invoking Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_Share on WS-IT-08. Returned shares include ADMIN$, IPC$, C$ — all with the $-suffix that hides them from default enumeration.", "chain_reason": "$-suffix shares are 'hidden' in the SMB sense; correlation rule fires on hidden-share enumeration as a recon indicator."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Hidden system folders inspected (read-only)", "technique": "T1564", "what_happened": "At 03:14:38, Sysmon EID 1 / FileAccess events for C:\\ProgramData, C:\\Windows\\WinSxS, C:\\Users\\<user>\\AppData\\Local — all are read-only attribute queries (Get-Item -Force), not file creation or modification.", "chain_reason": "These folders carry Hidden attribute by Windows design, but a read-only inspection is consistent with audit."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "ADS enumeration on user profile (read-only)", "technique": "T1564.004", "what_happened": "At 03:15:12, Sysmon EID 1 captures Get-Item -Stream * read of files under %USERPROFILE% — checking for unusual ADS streams. NO Sysmon EID 15 (FileCreateStreamHash) fires in this run.", "chain_reason": "Reading ADS metadata != creating ADS streams. EID 15 is the write-side indicator; EID 1 with -Stream * is the read-side audit."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Outlook EnableUnsafeClientMailRules read across Office versions (read-only)", "technique": "T1564.008", "what_happened": "At 03:15:42, Sysmon EID 13 reports reg-value-set events on HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Office\\{14.0,15.0,16.0}\\Outlook\\Security\\EnableUnsafeClientMailRules — all return DWORD (0x00000000) — value remains 0 across all versions.", "chain_reason": "Reading the key value != setting it to 1. Sysmon EID 13 captures both, but the details field shows the value is unchanged at 0."}
  ],
